{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T19:11:52.771Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"9156b995-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"narration-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 180,\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-734c-9be4-e150aeb4f01e\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Many believers know righteousness as God's gift, and that is true.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"27f538fc-9519-76f8-9022-da2e14ff8e7c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"But Paul also describes a harvest of righteousness that grows from what we actually do.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"27f538fc-9519-76f8-9022-da2e14ff8e7c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So here is the tension: how can something be both a gift and a harvest? This lesson resolves it.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"27f538fc-9519-76f8-9022-da2e14ff8e7c\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-7f48-aaa0-ac40dd9b090e\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Scripture shows us two manifestations of righteousness.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The first is righteousness given by God as a gift, available to everyone who believes.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The second is righteousness as a harvest, which comes on account of your obedience.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So the two differ in origin: one is received freely, while the other is produced through what you do.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Yet the harvest is not a prerequisite for your relationship with God.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Instead, it is the indistinguishable fruit of that relationship, the visible evidence that the relationship is real.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a6","textChunks":["{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"narration-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 180,\n  \"blocks\": [\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-734c-9be4-e150aeb4f01e\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Many believers know righteousness as God's gift, and that is true.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"27f538fc-9519-76f8-9022-da2e14ff8e7c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"But Paul also describes a harvest of righteousness that grows from what we actually do.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"27f538fc-9519-76f8-9022-da2e14ff8e7c\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So here is the tension: how can something be both a gift and a harvest? This lesson resolves it.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"27f538fc-9519-76f8-9022-da2e14ff8e7c\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-7f48-aaa0-ac40dd9b090e\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Scripture shows us two manifestations of righteousness.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The first is righteousness given by God as a gift, available to everyone who believes.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The second is righteousness as a harvest, which comes on account of your obedience.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"So the two differ in origin: one is received freely, while the other is produced through what you do.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Yet the harvest is not a prerequisite for your relationship with God.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Instead, it is the indistinguishable fruit of that relationship, the visible evidence that the relationship is real.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a6","60-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Think of it like an apple tree: you did not earn the tree, but its fruit proves the tree is alive and yours.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"analogy\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Helps learners grasp how the harvest flows from the relationship rather than earning it.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-7400-81f8-1bdabf1db446\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Paul makes this concrete in 2 Corinthians 9, using the language of farming.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"He writes, \\\"whoever sows sparingly will also reap sparingly, and whoever sows bountifully will also reap bountifully.\\\"\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"],\n          \"quotation\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"He adds that each person should give as decided in the heart, because God loves a cheerful giver.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"God is able to make grace abound so that you have sufficiency and can overflow in every good work.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Then comes the key promise: the one who supplies seed to the sower will multiply your seed and increase the harvest of your righteousness.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Notice the connection: sowing and generous giving are exactly what cause this harvest to grow.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-7cd0-9684-0ca56ec61208\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"There is also a diffe","rence of direction to see here.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Vertically, before God, all human efforts are like filthy rags, and every crown is cast down at his throne.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Horizontally, before people, faith can only be seen through visible works.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"David illustrates this beautifully.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"To Goliath, he spoke of covenant privilege, declaring his confidence in God.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"But to King Saul, he presented a practical resume: he had killed the lion and the bear.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-7bd7-967d-ee218134ee94\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The Hebrew word tzedakah captures this fuller picture of righteousness.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ae46abef-303d-74c7-aaed-ae3b93115a06\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"It has three dimensions.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ae46abef-303d-74c7-aaed-ae3b93115a06\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"First, personal morality: adhering to moral conduct, avoiding sin, and maintaining personal purity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6353155b-4af1-7602-beb9-ba44a3752dac\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Second, justice: standing up for the oppressed and vulnerable.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"54b12e03-243c-7c0a-b6f9-56810778b4e4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The Good Samaritan shows this: the religious leaders had positional righteousness but lacked active justice.\",","\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"54b12e03-243c-7c0a-b6f9-56810778b4e4\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Third, charity: being rich toward God and caring for the needy.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"08211261-1830-7557-9461-ea0c129d2a58\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"James points to Abraham: he was justified by faith, yet when he offered Isaac, his faith was perfected by works.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"08211261-1830-7557-9461-ea0c129d2a58\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-72d0-b9c8-e7577076167a\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Let's check what you've taken in.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [],\n          \"generatedAddition\": {\n            \"kind\": \"clarification\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Signals the transition into recall questions.\"\n          }\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"First, what distinguishes righteousness as a gift from righteousness as a harvest?\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Second, in 2 Corinthians 9, what increases the harvest of your righteousness?\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Third, name the three dimensions of tzedakah and one illustration of each.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"6353155b-4af1-7602-beb9-ba44a3752dac\", \"54b12e03-243c-7c0a-b6f9-56810778b4e4\", \"08211261-1830-7557-9461-ea0c129d2a58\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"outlineItemId\": \"01a14b42-669f-780f-b193-b077d5ff7973\",\n      \"sentences\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Righteousness is received as God's gift, yet we are called to work it out as a harvest through obedience, sowing, and giving.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\", \"679469fb-589a-7a5a-9a19-e707aa9eb8b5\"]\n        },\n        {\n          \"text\": \"This harvest flows from relationship with God, is visible before people, and takes shape in tz","edakah: morality, justice, and charity.\",\n          \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"ddd8a660-bfd1-71fb-bad2-44b3fca1b2c1\", \"2af4b3fd-3236-7fe7-b029-ff96a9ea899f\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":8180,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":42041,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a14b46-6fa0-7c1b-a916-ecf0af1ddd06"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T19:11:52.833Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.request","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","request":{"model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","messages":[{"role":"system","contentCharacters":1331},{"role":"user","contentCharacters":9523},{"role":"user","contentCharacters":2071}],"responseFormat":"json_object","hasJsonSchema":false,"temperature":null,"maxOutputTokens":"[REDACTED]","stream":true},"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a14b46-6fa0-7c1b-a916-ecf0af1ddd06"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-17T19:11:59.271Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"ba35f863-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"{\"repairs\":[{\"blockIndex\":3,\"sentenceIndex\":1,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"On the vertical level, standing before God, everything people achieve on their own counts for nothing — our best efforts fall short, and every crown gets laid down at his throne.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":3,\"sentenceIndex\":2,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"On the horizontal level, in front of other people, faith has to show up in actions you can actually observe, because that is the only way others can see it.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":4,\"sentenceIndex\":2,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"The first dimension is personal morality — living a clean life, steering clear of sin, and keeping yourself pure.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":4,\"sentenceIndex\":5,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"The third dimension is charity — being generous in your devotion to God and looking after those in need.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":4,\"sentenceIndex\":6,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"James holds up Abraham as the example: he was made right with God through faith, but when he placed Isaac on the altar, that faith reached its full completion through what he did.\"}]}]}","textChunks":["{\"repairs\":[{\"blockIndex\":3,\"sentenceIndex\":1,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"On the vertical level, standing before God, everything people achieve on their own counts for nothing — our best efforts fall short, and every crown gets laid down at his throne.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":3,\"sentenceIndex\":2,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"On the horizontal level, in front of other people, faith has to show up in actions you can actually observe, because that is the only way others can see it.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":4,\"sentenceIndex\":2,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"The first dimension is personal morality — living a clean life, steering clear of sin, and keeping yourself pure.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":4,\"sentenceIndex\":5,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"The third dimension is charity — being generous in your devotion to God and looking after those in need.\"}]},{\"blockIndex\":4,\"sentenceIndex\":6,\"sentences\":[{\"text\":\"James holds up Abraham as the example: he was made right with God through faith, but when he placed Isaac on the altar, that faith reached its full completion through what he did.\"}]}]}"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":1048,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":6433,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a14b46-6fa0-7c1b-a916-ecf0af1ddd06"}}
